page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-0-preparation","content":"About balloons:"},"176":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-33","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-0-preparation","content":"Balloons are usually printed by a receipt printer. Whenever a team solves a problem, a receipt is printed;"},"177":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-34","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-0-preparation","content":"The receipt contains team name, seat number, balloon color, all current balloon colors of that team, etc. Volunteers distribute balloons according to the receipt."},"178":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-35","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-0-preparation","content":"About automatic login:"},"179":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-36","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-0-preparation","content":"After enabling, users in the address list are automatically logged into the specified corresponding account. Users cannot log in again, cannot log out, and cannot log in from other IPs.\nBefore operating, make sure the list does not contain administrator accounts and IPs used by administrators!"},"180":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-37","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-0-preparation","content":"Optional:"},"181":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-38","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-0-preparation","content":"Install grafana and netdata to monitor server runtime status and show leadership;"},"182":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-39","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-1-warm-up-contest","content":"Warm-up contests usually use at least one problem that can be brute-forced with repeated submissions, guiding contestants to submit heavily and testing server load."},"183":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-40","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-2-official-contest","content":"If balloons are needed, inflate them early (usually the balloon group is very busy in the hour before the contest)"},"184":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-41","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-2-official-contest","content":"Remember to refill printer paper, same for receipt printers."},"185":{"id":"/en/docs/Tools-42","page_id":"/en/docs/Tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Tools#day-2-official-contest","content":"// TODO: scoreboard freeze configuration"},"186":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","type":"page","content":"Judge Communication Protocol","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge"},"187":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-0","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#judge-side-interaction-flow","content":"Judge-side Interaction Flow"},"188":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-1","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#websocket-connection-establishment-flow","content":"WebSocket Connection Establishment Flow"},"189":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-2","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#language-configuration-distribution","content":"Language Configuration Distribution"},"190":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-3","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#judge-task-push","content":"Judge Task Push"},"191":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-4","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#test-data-download","content":"Test Data Download"},"192":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-5","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#judge-result-reporting","content":"Judge Result Reporting"},"193":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-6","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","content":"Current version: v1."},"194":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-7","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#judge-side-interaction-flow","content":"GET /judge/files (check whether login status is valid; if invalid, enter login flow; usually executed once every six hours)"},"195":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-8","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#judge-side-interaction-flow","content":"WEBSOCKET /judge/conn (main interaction channel)"},"196":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-9","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#judge-side-interaction-flow","content":"If login has expired, perform login."},"197":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-10","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#websocket-connection-establishment-flow","content":"After the connection is established, the judge reports current node status to Web (optional)Note: the information below is only for data format demonstration and is not guaranteed to be real or valid."},"198":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-11","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#websocket-connection-establishment-flow","content":"After connection establishment, the judge sends {\"key\":\"ping\"} every 30s."},"199":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-12","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#language-configuration-distribution","content":"After the connection is established, the Web side distributes server-side language settings to the Judge. If the client needs special settings, this message can be ignored."},"200":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-13","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#judge-task-push","content":"The Web side pushes judge tasks to the judge side via WebSocket."},"201":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-14","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#judge-task-push","content":"Note 1: if contest ID is 000000000000000000000000, this submission is a custom test submission, and the custom test uses the input field as program input.Note 2: the source field is a cache ID; submissions with the same source field use the same cache directory.Note 3: the source field contains exactly one character /; domainId/pid is recommended.Note 4: the etag of test data is used to identify whether local cached files are consistent with the cloud; you can use a hash or a modified-time timestamp."},"202":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-15","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#test-data-download","content":"If test data used in the pushed judge task is missing, the Judge side requests missing or modified files from Web."},"203":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-16","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#test-data-download","content":"The server returns:"},"204":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge-17","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/Hydro/api/judge#judge-result-reporting","content":"Except for the three fields key, domainId, and rid, all other fields are optional. For STATUS_CODE meanings, see hydro-dev/Hydro/packages/utils/lib/status.When key is end, it means the judge task is completed and the result is finalized. The Web side can then count ACs, register scoreboards, and perform related operations."},"205":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ/debug","page_id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ/debug","type":"page","content":"Debugging Guide","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Hydro","FAQ"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ/debug"},"206":{"id":"/en/docs/Hydro/FAQ/d